{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task. I need to implement a `solve(case)` function for task AGENT-TF-01.\n\nLooking at the fixtures, each case has:\n- `threshold`: a float (e.g., 0.05)\n- `calls`: a list of call objects, each with:\n  - `call_id`: string\n  - `loss_without_call`: float\n  - `loss_with_call`: float\n  - `prediction_tokens`: int\n  - `parseable`: boolean\n\nThe output needs:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted` (bool), `call_id` (str), `normalized_gain` (float)\n\nI need to figure out what \"normalized_gain\" means and when a call is \"accepted\".\n\nThe gain from a call is `loss_without_call - loss_with_call` (positive means the call helped).\n\nThe \"normalized\" part likely means normalizing by the number of prediction tokens: `(loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens`.\n\nA call is \"accepted\" if:\n1. It's parseable (`parseable == true`)\n2. The normalized gain exceeds the threshold\n\nLet me verify with the fixture data:\n\nCase 000:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, normalized = 1.56265595 / 5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → accepted (0.31253119 \u003e 0.05)\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, normalized = 0.37796304 / 4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted (0.09449076 \u003e 0.05)\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, normalized = 0.74550131 / 6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, normalized = 0.7595393 / 5 = 0.1519079 (wait, let me recalculate: 0.7595393/5 = 0.15190786), parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, normalized = 0.20983801 / 5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true → NOT accepted (0.041... \u003c 0.05)\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, normalized = 0.76393214 / 4 = 0.190983035, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo for case 000: accepted = call0, call1, call2, call3, call5; rejected = call4\n\nCase 002 has call4 with parseable=false, so it should be rejected regardless of gain.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis seems reasonable. The normalized gain is per-token loss improvement, and a call is accepted if it's parseable and the normalized gain exceeds the threshold.\n\nNow I need to return this as a JSON object with `\"implementation\"` key containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01V1Um0uPBzjfBibEE518flQ","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2125,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":92,"output_tokens":1275,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1028},"service_tier":"standard"}}